Configuring Environment variables 

Ways of defining environment variables 

1. env: 
     - key: <name>
       value: <value>

2. configMap 
   imperative way 
     kubectl create configmap <config_name> --from-literal=APP=MY_APP --from-literal=COLOR=ORANGE
     kubectl create configmap <config_name> --from-file=<file_path>

   declarative way 
     Using defination file

   Injecting ways
a.  envFrom 
b.  env: 
    key: key_name
    valueFrom: 
     configMapRef:
        name: <config_name>
        key: <key_name>
c.  volumes: 
     name: config_vols
     configMap: 
       name: <config_name>     , stored as key = file_name  , value = content of file in mountPath defination

